    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T20:28:45Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/1963-envelope-table · PR #2006 · pinned by mill_envelope_stands_on_table_for_all_travel_files and mill_envelope_stays_on_table_with_shifted_origin_and_inverted_z · merges when reviewed\n\nThe defect is in the viewport display only.\nNo travel, reach, collision, or posting check uses the drawn box.\nThe travel check reads axis limits and program coordinates directly.\nThe effort label stays effort:medium.\n\nThe reading uses assets/machines/tormach-pcnc1100-s3.mch with the fresh document implicit setup and default G54 origin.\nThe old bottom was Z=-419.1 mm. The new bottom is Z=0 mm.\nThe library pin checks all box envelopes with complete travel limits.\nX/Y keep their setup origin reference. The table plane does not define a footprint for a different X/Y reference.\nThe second pin checks G54 at [10, 20, 70] mm and inverted Z.\n\nBoth pins failed before the fix.\nBoth failed again with the original module restored from upstream/main.\nBoth passed after I restored the fix.\nThe quick gate and clippy passed. No goldens changed.\n",
